                <pb facs="0097" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/1402: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-02-11T15:00:00-05:00">February 11, 1939—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. For Myron Taylor. Your 198, February 10, 1 p.m. As in the case of the
                    Sudetens, we are reluctant to see the Committee’s problem increased but, also as
                    in the case of the Sudetens, the Poles in question are unquestionably
                    involuntary emigrants from Germany and thus appear to come within the
                    Committee’s competence.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
